From ebde9c724a8cff2542d1818280a4bad684c71693 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 06:30:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban OOM follow-ups to #1804: victim lookup after
 a restart, bounded journal read, honest 137 attribution

Review nits on #1804 (reviews 5884824785, 5885069810, 5886864029):

- read_failure looks up the kernel's OOM victim restricted to the worker pid
  whenever the pid is known. It used to need this process's probe verdict
  (_oom_continue_supported), so a dispatcher restarted between spawn and the
  agent's own OOM death (no snapshot after SIGKILL, --collect scope GC'd)
  booked a generic crash and the retry's memory cap was not doubled.
- The kernel-log read runs inside the reclaim write txn, so it is bounded by
  the run's start (journalctl -S @<task_runs.started_at>) instead of -24h.
- OomWatch no longer pins a concurrent job's OOM kill on the foreground
  command: it reads the kernel's victim since the command started. A victim
  already in the run scope before the command gets a note naming it and no
  claim about the command; no kernel record gives a hedged "exited by SIGKILL
  while the OOM killer fired" note. A survivable command's own transient scope
  is checked too (its kill never moved the run scope's count).
- A call-site comment and a compute-policy test pin that OOMPolicy=continue is
  added before bounded_scope's `-- nice -n 15`, where apply_toolchain_env
  finds it.
- Docstring reflow in tools/process_registry_persist_scope.py.
